                "text": "Analyse the examples:\nEach input has a few single non-zero colored pixels.\nLooking at the outputs:\nFor each colored pixel at (r, c):\n- It extends to the right until the right edge of the grid: from (r, c) to (r, width-1).\n- Then it extends downwards along the rightmost column (col = width - 1) until either:\n  - the next colored pixel's row (or does it? Wait, in example 1:\n    - 2 at (1,2): goes to (1, 7). Then col 7 has 2 at rows 2, 3. At row 4, color 4 is at (4,1). Col 7 has 4 at rows 4, 5.\n    - 7 at (6,5): goes to (6, 7). Col 7 has 7 at rows 6, 7, 8 (until the bottom!).\n    - Wait, does each color extend down along the right column until the next color's row?\n    - Let's check:\n      - 2: row 1 to 3 (row 4 has 4).\n      - 4: row 4 to 5 (row 6 has 7).\n      - 7: row 6 to 8 (end of grid).\n    - Example 3:\n      - 6 at row 0: right to col 9. Col 9: rows 0, 1. (Row 2 has 1).\n      - 1 at row 2: right to col 9. Col 9: rows 2, 3. (Row 4 has 3).\n      - 3 at row 4: right to col 9. Col 9: rows 4, 5. (Row 6 has 9).\n      - 9 at row 6: right to col 9. Col 9: row 6. (End of grid).\n    - Example 4:\n      - 4 at row 1: rightmost col 6, rows 1, 2, 3. (Row 4 has 5).\n      - 5 at row 4: rightmost col 6, rows 4, 5, 6, 7. (Row 8 has 2).\n      - 2 at row 8: rightmost col 6, rows 8, 9, 10. (End of grid).\n    - Example 2:\n      - 8 at row 2: right to col 5. Col 5: rows 2, 3, 4, 5, 6. (End of grid).\n\nSo the rule is:\n1. Sort colored pixels by their row index in ascending order.\n2. For the i-th pixel at (r_i, c_i) with color C_i:\n   - Fill row r_i from column c_i to width - 1 with color C_i.\n   - Fill the rightmost column (width - 1) from row r_i to r_{i+1} - 1 (or height - 1 if it's the last pixel) with color C_i.\n\nEverything else stays 0.\n\nReady for test input.All insights collected. Ready for test inputs!",
